14. Validation

Validation means checking whether the user's input is acceptable.

For example:

Name cannot be empty.
Age must be a number.
Email cannot be empty.
Password must be long enough.

A simple validation example:

function handleSubmit(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    if (name === "") {
        console.log("Name is required");
        return;
    }

    console.log("Form submitted");
}

You can also store an error message in state.

const [error, setError] = useState("");

function handleSubmit(e) {
    e.preventDefault();

    if (name === "") {
        setError("Name is required");
        return;
    }

    setError("");
}

Then display it:

{error && <p>{error}</p>}

This combines validation with conditional rendering.

Multiple validation rules
if (name === "") {
    setError("Name is required");
} else if (name.length < 3) {
    setError("Name must have at least 3 characters");
} else {
    setError("");
}
