Delete a todo.
Edit a todo.

Don't worry about a database yet. Keep everything in React state.

16. Search and Filtering

Once an application has many items, users need a way to find specific items.

Search usually works by storing the search text in state.

const [search, setSearch] = useState("");

Then filter the data:

const filteredProducts = products.filter(product =>
    product.name
        .toLowerCase()
        .includes(search.toLowerCase())
);

Then display:

{filteredProducts.map(product => (
    <ProductCard
        key={product.id}
        product={product}
    />
))}
How it works

If the products are:

Keyboard
Mouse
Monitor
Headset

and the user searches:

mouse

the filtered result becomes:

Mouse
Filtering by category

Search isn't the only type of filtering.

For example:

const filteredProducts = products.filter(product =>
    product.category === selectedCategory
);

You can also combine conditions:

const filteredProducts = products.filter(product =>
    product.name.toLowerCase().includes(search.toLowerCase()) &&
    product.category === selectedCategory
);
